bin/
knowledge.db
knowledge.db-*
.env

# Vendored CDN assets — fetch with `make vendor`, never commit (the .gitkeep is tracked
# so //go:embed always has a match).
web/vendor/*
!web/vendor/.gitkeep

# Build-time-only tool cache (mermaid for `make diagram`) — never a dependency
# of the product, so it is fetched on demand and not committed.
.cache/

# The dev corpus. `docs/` is CORPUS_DIR's default, so it is where a real document
# lands the moment anyone runs `make ingest` or imports through the app on a laptop —
# and this repository is public. Track the folder, never its contents: a deployment
# keeps its corpus in a private repo of its own (see changelog/).
docs/*
!docs/.gitkeep

# web/ui is a Vite project: its dependencies are fetched, its *output* is committed.
# web/dist is deliberately NOT ignored — the binary embeds it, which is what keeps
# `go build` and a deploy free of Node (CLAUDE.md rule 14).
web/ui/node_modules/

# One package manager. CI installs with `npm ci`, so package-lock.json is the tree the
# committed bundle is built from; a pnpm lockfile resolving anything differently makes rule
# 14's rebuild-and-diff compare a bundle built from other dependencies. It also carries a
# sha512 per entry, so `make secrets` reports it as a credential — which is how it announced
# itself both times it was committed.
web/ui/pnpm-lock.yaml
